---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import backgroundImage from "../images/bio-background-image.jpg";
import bioImage from "../images/bio-image.jpg";
---

<section class="biography-section">
  <div class="image-section-container">
    <div class="background-image-container">
      <Image class="background-image" src={backgroundImage} alt="Colorful painting of a horse and rider." format="avif" widths={[800, 400]} quality="50" />
    </div>
    <Image class="bio-image img-card" src={bioImage} alt="Carole Nylander leaning next to two of her oil paintings." format="avif" width={640} />
  </div>
  <div class="text-content-container">
    <div class="text-content">
      <div class="bio-heading">
        <h2>Biography</h2>
        <div class="line"></div>
      </div>
      <p>
        Creation of art has been a passion for me all my life. After working disparate jobs, I always return to creating art.
      </p>
      <p>
        Born in Los Angeles, my earliest years were spent in a little farming town in Northern Iowa. From there my family moved to Ogden, Utah. In high school I won an art scholarship to Pepperdine University in California. One semester I attended the University of Guadalajara in Mexico before returning to graduate from Weber State University in Ogden with a degree in art education.
      </p>
      <p>
        I was a teacher in the Pacific Northwest for a while before returning to Ogden where I married a history teacher/newspaper reporter. We were blessed with twin daughters. I showed my paintings and taught art classes at Eccles Art Center. 
      </p>
      <p>
        Changing careers to court reporting, I worked in Salt Lake City courts -- such an interesting place to observe human nature! Then with a computer ability to write 165 wpm, I wrote 25+ people’s biographies. I also took notes for conferences of the National Alliance for Mental Illness and other organizations.
      </p>
      <p>
        All those places of work reminded me of my need to create something of beauty or of interest and intrigue. The process is healing and positive.
      </p>
      <p>
        The National Ephemera Society is a help for me with my (paper) antique/historical collection. Some of the ideas and artwork in old periodicals are astonishing. We Americans can learn so much about ourselves from our 250+ years of paper trail – more accurately than from school history books. I did a show of ephemeral art at the Weber County Library and had a radio interview.
      </p>
      <p>
        Now that I’m living in North County San Diego, I show my paintings at the North Coastal Art Gallery, the Escondido Art Association and sometimes at the Brooks Theatre. In my first year back in California, I won a first-place blue ribbon for an oil painting, followed by eight more ribbons in the next few years.
      </p>
      <p>
        I have sold paintings all over the Western U.S. One of my largest paintings of cowboy James Dean hangs in a doctors’ office in Canberra, Australia.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style lang="scss">
  @use "../styles/column-layouts" as *;
  @use "../styles/breakpoints" as *;

  section {
    padding-top: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 5fr 7fr;
  }

  .image-section-container {
    padding-left: var(--side-margin);
    padding-top: 140px;
    position: relative;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: end;
  }

  .background-image-container {
    position: absolute;
    width: calc(100% - col-width(1));
    height: 100%;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    z-index: -1;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .background-image {
    filter: blur(2px);
    transform: scale(1.2);
    height: 100%;
  }

  .bio-image {
    max-width: col-width(4);
    aspect-ratio: 3/4;
    height: min-content;
  }

  .text-content-container {
    padding-left: var(--section-gap);
    padding-right: var(--side-margin);
    padding-top: 312px;
    width: 100%;
  }

  .text-content {
    max-width: col-width(5);
  }

  .bio-heading {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 5rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
  }

  .line {
    width: 100%;
    height: 1px;
    background-color: var(--border-color);
  }

  p {
    color: var(--subtle-text);
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }

  @media screen and (max-width: $breakpoint-md) {
    section {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .background-image-container {
      width: 100%;
    }
    .background-image {
      width: 100%;
    }
    .image-section-container {
      padding-left: 0;
      padding-top: 0;
      justify-content: center;
    }
    .text-content-container {
      display: flex;
      justify-content: center;
      padding-inline: var(--side-margin);
      padding-top: var(--section-padding);
    }
  }
</style>